{"title":"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider two externally tangent circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> with centers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> have radii of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. There exist points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/1375da8b94d688b4928311f04d35a57081ee0f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are the external tangents of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />. The circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1c31c047878777dfc62f72efef75924195715d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BO_2D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a6153b31b4bc98f72ed128a47fa0fd4b3563381a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX &lt; AY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73205379672e860eb250c541187600fae3a3e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb3bd49db3f0869867e44ebe0b5a0dd6c2a6294a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{m}}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fbe77c4364e283fa0ecd4e8c647216365060b94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); pair A = (-1/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair B = (-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2); pair C = (5/2,3*sqrt(3)/2); pair D = (5/2,-3*sqrt(3)/2); pair O1 = (0,0); pair O2 = (4,0); pair O3 = (7/4,-sqrt(3)/4); pair X = (1/4,3*sqrt(3)/4); pair Y = (1,sqrt(3)); pair P = (-2,0); pair Q = (-1/2,0); pair R = (5/2,sqrt(3));  draw(B--D); draw(circle(O1,1)); draw(circle(O2,3)); draw(circle(O3,sqrt(21)/2),blue+dashed); draw(O1--A--C--O2--cycle,dashed+magenta); draw(A--B,dashed+red); draw(C--D,dashed+red);  dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); dot(&quot;$O_1$&quot;,O1,NE); dot(&quot;$O_2$&quot;,O2,NE); dot(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,N); dot(&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,N); dot(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,NW); dot(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,SW); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"355\" /> </center><p> Firstly, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738afb7c28af62ea71abfdf41851e5371a10c3c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC=\\sqrt{(O_1O_2)^2-(CO_2-AO_1)^2}=\\sqrt{4^2-(3-1)^2}=2\\sqrt{3}.\\]\" width=\"474\" height=\"32\" /> It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6bd204e29ea6963238b53f849b5f58cddfd955c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB=\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad CD=3\\sqrt{3}.\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" /> Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> with the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1c31c047878777dfc62f72efef75924195715d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BO_2D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/5/e3522762222ab5c37a965916249472edd01273fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BQO_2D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae13caa51a60fa25a7f21ee01f6b945e74498777.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BQO_2 = 180-\\angle BDO_2 = 180^{\\circ} - 90^{\\circ} = 90^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"16\" /> So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfb915a584a9bf89ae73b93dd0befb7cc2913424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"43\" />. By symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23afff10e401eafc8ef79c6f12b3d5d58dcd9f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ=CR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />. From the power of a point and segment addition, we have \\begin{align*} (AX)(AY) = (AX)(AX+XY) &amp;= (AQ)(AB) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot\\sqrt{3} \\\\ (CY)(CX) = (CY)(XY+YC) &amp;= (CR)(CD) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ AX+XY+YC &amp;= AC = 2\\sqrt{3}. \\end{align*} Solving, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e8fae104d6081bb4af286f14e27e838b607f2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec09c4f98473da49d3a49822e2b707d807fa485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/5625c8b6a328550a0c2494e6a92f1a44a0ce42ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YC=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/85562194f091f350e74e53f9be104c44bb0a1ac4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CX=XY+YC=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\sqrt{3}=\\frac{\\sqrt{27}}{2}\\implies 27+2=\\boxed{29}.\\]\" width=\"453\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017024548\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 189/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8634/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26215:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017024548 and revision id 280175. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}